- [Recursive name servers](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/general-information/recursive-name-servers/): Hetzner's official recursive DNS server addresses, usage guide, and query source network ranges.
- [Server relocations](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/general-information/server-relocations/): Backup data and check hardware before server migrations to ensure safe relocation and minimal downtime.
- [Server transfers between Robot customers](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/general-information/server-transfers-between-robot-customers/): Guide for Hetzner Robot customers to transfer dedicated root servers via forum marketplace or direct token.
- [System adjustments after server replacement with transfer of the drives](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/general-information/system-adjustments-after-server-replacement/): Adjust network configuration after server replacement due to interface naming changes in supported Linux distributions.
- [Setting up a bare metal server for the first time](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/getting-started/setting-up-a-bare-metal-server-for-the-first-time/): Log into the Robot portal to manage your server's operating system, IP addresses, rescue system, and support requests.
- [Bare metal server overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/getting-started/root-server-guide/): Overview of dedicated server hardware, software, networking, and support management through the Robot administration interface.
- [Partition Alignment](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/getting-started/partition-alignment/): Explains partition alignment importance for storage performance and how operating systems handle automatic or manual configuration.
