- [IP Addresses](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/ip/ip-addresses/)
- [The basics of IPv4 and IPv6](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/ip/ip-basics/): Overview of IPv4 limitations, IPv6 development history, and current global adoption trends for network transition.
- [Getting Started](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/mac-mini/getting-started/)
- [Hot Swapping](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/maintenance/hot-swapping/): Check server hot-swap capability via the Robot interface under technical support settings.
- [IPMI](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/maintenance/ipmi/): Hetzner's IPMI policy, supported Dell models, security rationale, and steps to activate BMC network access with an additional IP address.
- [KVM Console](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/maintenance/kvm-console/): Hetzner provides free KVM-over-IP remote consoles for server troubleshooting, boot access, and ISO mounting across Lantronix and Raritan models.
- [NVMe](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/maintenance/nvme/): Explains UNIX/Linux NVMe device naming conventions, including controller, namespace, and partition identifiers.
- [Serial over LAN](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/maintenance/serial-over-lan/): Enable and configure Serial Over LAN via IPMI for remote Linux console and GRUB setup.
- [10G Uplink](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/10g-uplink/): Guide to upgrading dedicated servers to 10G uplinks, including pricing, traffic limits, firewall restrictions, and post-upgrade network configuration steps.
- [iDRAC: Switching from DHCP to static IP at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/idrac-server-dhcp-to-static/): Configure a static IP address using ipmitool or the web interface, with steps varying by iDRAC revision.
- [Network configuration CentOS](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/net-config-cent-os/): Configures IPv4 and IPv6 main addresses for dedicated root servers, including gateway setup and troubleshooting.
- [Network configuration Debian / Ubuntu](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/net-config-debian-ubuntu/): Configures main IPv4 address using point-to-point routing, /32 netmask, and explicit gateway routes in network settings.
- [Network configuration using systemd-networkd](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/network-configuration-using-systemd-networkd/)
- [Network configuration with Netplan](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/network-configuration-with-netplan/): Ubuntu netplan configuration guide for base setups, additional IPs, virtualization, and encrypted drive networking.
- [NetworkManager: Switching from DHCP to static IP at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/networkmanager-dhcp-to-static/): Guide to configuring Linux NetworkManager for static IPv4 and IPv6 addresses instead of DHCP.
- [vSwitch](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/vswitch/): Overview of Hetzner vSwitch: virtual layer 2 networks connecting dedicated servers across locations.
- [vSwitch for Windows servers](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/vswitch-windows/): Configure Hetzner vSwitch on Windows servers with VLAN setup, MTU adjustment, and Cloud-Network static routing.
- [Windows Server: Switching from DHCP to static IP at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/network/windows-server-dhcp-to-static/): Guide to configuring static IPv4 and IPv6 on Windows Server for Hetzner network changes.
- [cPanel](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/cpanel/): New cPanel/Plesk sales end January 2025. Existing license prices increase January 2026. Full pricing table provided.
- [Deactivate GRUB2 recordfail feature](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/deactivate-grub2-recordfail/): Disable GRUB2 recordfail feature and configure boot timeout via config files.
- [EFI system partition](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/efi-system-partition/): Guide to creating and configuring an EFI System Partition for UEFI boot on Linux and Windows.
- [Hang Up with Realtek r8169-r8168 NIC](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/realtek-r8169-r8168-nic/): Fix network hangs by disabling TCP segmentation offload via ethtool and installing the r8168-dkms driver for Realtek NICs.
- [Hetzner Debian/Ubuntu Package Mirror](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/hetzner-package-mirror/): Configure Hetzner's local Debian and Ubuntu package mirror to save bandwidth and speed up installations, with full IPv6 support.
- [Installimage](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/installimage/): Hetzner's installimage script enables fast Linux installation via Rescue System with customizable partitioning, RAID, and LVM configuration.
- [Installing custom images](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/installing-custom-images/): Covers three methods for installing custom or older operating systems on Hetzner servers using Installimage and KVM console.
- [Plesk](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/plesk/): Instructions for manual Plesk installation and link to Plesk documentation.
- [Standard images](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/standard-images/): Hetzner's installimage script installs various Linux distributions on dedicated servers with customized boot, network, and repository settings.
- [UEFI](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/uefi/): Default server deployment switches to UEFI boot, detailing benefits, verification methods, and compatibility limitations.
- [VNC install](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/operating-systems/vnc-install/): Learn how to perform VNC installations via Hetzner Robot using remote access and a VNC client.
- [3Ware RAID Controller](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/3ware-raid-controller/): Download, extract, and execute the 3ware tw_cli tool for managing RAID controllers on Linux or Rescue systems.
- [Adaptec hardware RAID controller](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/adaptec-raid-controller/): Use the arcconf command-line tool to check hardware RAID and drive status via GETCONFIG commands.
- [Exchanging hard disks in a Software-RAID](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/exchanging-hard-disks-in-a-software-raid/): Step-by-step guide for replacing a defective drive in a software RAID array using mdadm.
- [Linux Software RAID](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/linux-software-raid/): Use `cat /proc/mdstat` to check active software RAID arrays, view disk status, and monitor resync progress.
- [LSI RAID Controller](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/lsi-raid-controller/): Use megacli commands to check hardware RAID controller status, logical drives, and physical drive health.
- [Partition size limit on big hard drives](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/partitions-size-limit-on-big-hard-drives/): GPT partition tables enable booting and bypass the 2TB MS-DOS limit via the installimage script.
- [RAID](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/raid/): How to identify Hetzner server RAID controller (LSI, Adaptec, 3Ware) using lspci and links to controller guides.
- [Software-RAID](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/software-raid/): Guide to installing, configuring, and removing software RAID, including drive failure notifications and system commands.
- [Windows Server Software RAID](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/raid/windows-server-software-raid/): Open Disk Management, prepare drives, convert to dynamic, and verify Legacy or UEFI mode.
- [NTP Servers](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/security/ntp-servers/): Hetzner NTP servers for accurate time synchronization, including server addresses and configuration guide.
- [SSH](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/security/ssh/): Learn how to access SSH servers on Hetzner products and install the SSH service on various operating systems.
- [System Monitor (SysMon)](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/security/system-monitor/): Configure Hetzner Server Monitoring to track services, set checks, manage contacts, and receive email alerts for status changes.
- [Apple and RX Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/apple-rx-server/): Overview of discontinued Apple and RX server models, guaranteed minimum specs, available add-ons and upgrade limitations.
- [AX Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/ax-server/): Overview of configurable Hetzner AX server models, storage, RAM, NIC add-ons, and upgrade options (prices separate).
- [DS Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/ds-server/): Documentation of discontinued DS server models, their non-upgradable hardware, and available add-ons (NIC, USB, IP options).
- [DX Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/dx-server/): Overview of DX (Dell) server model configurations, upgrade options (RAM, drives, NICs) and minimum guaranteed specs.
- [EQ Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/eq-server/): Documentation of discontinued EQ server models, fixed hardware configs, no RAM/drive upgrades, NIC add-ons available.
- [EX Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/ex-server/): Overview of configurable Hetzner EX server models, drive/RAM upgrade options, and available hardware add-ons.
- [GPU Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/gpu-server/): Overview of configurable GEX GPU servers: base specs, RAM/drive/NIC upgrade options, add-ons, and technical limitations.
- [PX Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/px-server/): Documentation of deprecated PX server models, their guaranteed configs, drive/RAM upgrade options, and available add‑ons.
- [SX Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/sx-server/): Overview of SX server models, guaranteed minimums, RAM/drive upgrade options, and available network and hardware add-ons.
- [X and XS Server – Possible configurations and add-ons](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/server-lines/x-xs-server/): List of X and XS server models, fixed hardware options, available add-ons (NICs, USB, IPs) and upgrade notes.
- [Securing open reflectors](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/securing-open-reflectors/): Overview of all chapters: Reflection attacks, reading the report, securing DNS, SNMP, CLDAP, portmap, memcached, chargen, NTP, RDP, WS-Discovery, and FAQs.
- [Change boot order](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/change-boot-order/): Resolve RHEL 9 network boot failure by reordering UEFI boot entries using efibootmgr.
- [Filesystem check](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/filesystem-check/): Learn to identify partitions, configure automatic checks, and run manual Linux filesystem consistency checks, including LVM snapshot procedures.
- [Guideline for locked products](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/guideline-in-case-of-server-locking/): Reasons for product locking include non-payment, abuse, and network attacks to protect infrastructure and server owners.
- [Hetzner Rescue System](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/hetzner-rescue-system/): Guide to Hetzner Rescue System: network-boot live environment for recovery, mounting drives, LVM, chroot password reset, and OS install.
- [Instructions for an error report with Hetzner network problems](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/network-diagnosis-and-report-to-hetzner/): Restart your server via Robot or check for locking. Submit a support ticket if the issue persists.
- [Microsoft Blacklist](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/microsoft-blacklist/): Explains Microsoft OLC blacklisting, S3140/S3150 error codes, throttling limits, and manual IP delisting procedures.
- [Performance with Intel i218/i219 NIC](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/performance-intel-i218-nic/): Resolve Intel i218/i219 NIC performance issues on Linux 4.15+ by disabling TCP segmentation offloading via ethtool.
- [Recovery of LVM Volumes](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/recovery-of-lvm-volumes/): Step-by-step guide to recover missing LVM volumes and data from backups on Linux.
- [Serial numbers and information on defective hard drives](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/troubleshooting/serial-numbers-and-information-on-defective-hard-drives/): Learn to retrieve drive serial numbers on Windows, Linux, and FreeBSD using command-line tools and DiskID32.
- [General](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/virtualization/general/): Configure additional IPs and subnets for virtualization using bridged, routed, or NAT modes and virtual MACs.
- [VKVM](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/virtualization/vkvm/): vKVM boots your server OS in a VM to fix boot issues, passing storage and network access while restricting ports.
- [VMware ESXi](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/virtualization/vmware-esxi/): Covers ESXi compatibility, bridged networking, installation basics, and license activation on Hetzner servers.
- [Windows Server HyperV](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/virtualization/windows-server-hyperv/): Configure additional single IPs for Hyper-V VMs using virtual MAC addresses and external virtual switches.
- [Changing the Windows password during first login](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/changing-windows-password/): Network Level Authentication prevents forced Windows password changes on first login by executing before session creation.
- [Microsoft Hyper-V Network Configuration](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/microsoft-hyper-v-network-configuration/): Configure Hyper-V networks, assign single IPs via virtual MAC addresses, and set up virtual switches for VM connectivity.
- [Windows In-place-Upgrades](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/inplace-upgrades/): Windows Server 2019/2022 to 2025 in-place upgrades via specific KBs, not Windows Update, requiring Robot re-install.
- [Windows Server 2008 R2](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-2008/): Learn to configure Windows Server RAID 1 mirroring for automatic drive redundancy and data protection.
- [Windows Server 2012](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-2012/): Order the Windows Server add-on via Robot for automatic installation and email confirmation.
- [Windows Server 2016](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-2016/): Order the Windows Server 2016 add-on via Robot for automatic installation and email confirmation.
- [Windows Server 2019](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-2019/): Order the Windows Server 2019 add-on via Robot for automatic installation and email confirmation.
- [Windows Server 2022](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-2022/): Order the Windows Server 2022 add-on via Robot for automatic server installation and email confirmation.
- [Windows Server 2025](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-2025/): Order the Windows Server 2025 add-on via Robot for automatic installation and email notification.
- [Windows Server IIS](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-iis/): Step-by-step guide to installing Microsoft IIS on Windows Server via graphical interface and command line.
- [Windows Server Subnet](https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/dedicated-server/windows-server/windows-server-subnet/): Install DHCP and Hyper-V roles via Server Manager while skipping initial virtual switch creation.

