### SSL

- [General information](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/general-information/): Manage SSL accounts for encrypted domain connections using SNI or dedicated IPs via the SSL Manager.
- [Add a Certificate to an SSL Account](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/ssl-accounts/): Install a ready-to-use SSL certificate via the SSL Manager to enable encrypted HTTPS access.
- [Requesting a Free Basic or Let's Encrypt Certificate    ](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/ssl-guide/): Request a free Basic or Let's Encrypt certificate in the SSL Manager of konsoleH with automatic installation of the SSL account.
- [Importing a Third-Party Certificate](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/import-certificate/): Import a third-party SSL certificate into the konsoleH SSL Manager. Generate a CSR and private key using OpenSSL, use PEM format, unencrypted private key, intermediate and root certificates, and use it with an SSL account.
- [Managing certificates in the SSL Manager](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/manage-certificates/): Renew a Business certificate in the konsoleH SSL Manager. Hetzner sends a reminder about four weeks before expiration, the renewal process is like placing a new order, and then the certificate must be activated.
- [Order a Business Certificate](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/order-business-certificate/): Instructions for ordering a paid Thawte Business Certificate in the konsoleH SSL Manager.
- [Shortening the validity period of SSL certificates](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/shortening-of-validity-period/): Explains SSL certificate validity reductions and need for automation due to shorter maximum lifetimes.
- [SSL certificates in konsoleH](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/ssl/certificates/): Hetzner provides Basic, Let’s Encrypt, and Business SSL certificates with various validation levels, managed via konsoleH or third-party imports.

