- [Webserver configuration on konsoleH](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/webserver-configuration-konsoleh/): Protect a directory with username and password via konsoleH; add, change, or delete users.
- [Blocked User Agents](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/blocked-user-agents/): Lists default blocked AI and web crawlers like GPTBot and ClaudeBot, explaining their typical data collection purposes.
- [Configure HTTPS, Caching, and Security with .htaccess](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/https-caching-security-configuration/): Redirect all HTTP requests to HTTPS using .htaccess rewrite rules for permanent 301 redirects.
- [CORS configuration](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/cors/): Guide to configuring CORS headers (.htaccess) including methods, origins, headers and OPTIONS preflight handling.
- [Enable web server extensions on konsoleH](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/activate-extensions/): List of available web server extensions and their purposes (HTTP/2, Deflate, Pagespeed, Brotli).
- [PHP configuration](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/php-configuration/): Set default PHP version and file extension mappings; .htaccess examples for per-directory PHP versions and CLI commands.
- [Sending SMSs with konsoleH](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/sms/): Overview of konsoleH SMS features: send messages, notifications, website integration, and sent/active summaries.
- [Use CGI Scripts](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/cgi-scripts/): Place your CGI script inside public_html, e.g., public_html/cgi-bin/script.cgi; extensions like .pl may apply.
- [Use custom PEAR packages](https://docs.hetzner.com/managed/webserver/use-custom-pear-packages/): Explains SSH requirement for setting up a local PEAR repository or uploading PEAR packages manually.

## Network & Security

### Networks

- [Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/overview/): Overview of private Networks: private IPs, dedicated interfaces, subnets, routes, vSwitch, and internet access via public IP.
- [Connect Dedicated Servers (vSwitch)](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/connect-dedi-vswitch/): Explains linking Hetzner Cloud Networks and dedicated root server vSwitches for private network connectivity.
- [FAQ](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/faq/): Private layer 3 links between Hetzner cloud servers for multi-tier architectures across locations.
- [Hetzner Cloud Networks Configuration](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/server-configuration/): Download and install hc-utils package with distro-specific commands for Debian, RHEL, and Fedora variants.
- [Creating a Network](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/getting-started/creating-a-network/): Guide to creating and attaching a private Network in Hetzner Console, including naming and RFC1918 IP ranges.
- [Architecture](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/technical-concepts/architecture/): Explains Layer 2 vSwitch (on-link) and Layer 3 Cloud subnet (routed) communication with ARP/gateway examples.
- [Terminology](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/technical-concepts/terminology/): Explains MTU, MSS and added private network headers; shows MTU/MSS differences for HTTP, FTP, and ping.
- [MTU](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/networks/troubleshooting/mtu/): Guide to test and fix MTU/Path MTU Discovery issues using ping, tcpdump, MTU settings, and MSS clamping.

### Load Balancers

- [Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/load-balancers/overview/): Overview of Load Balancers: traffic distribution, availability, Round Robin and Least Connections algorithms, IPv4/IPv6 support.
- [FAQ](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/load-balancers/faq/): Explains load balancer purpose: distributes traffic for availability, scalability, performance; lists public/private IPv4 and IPv6 presence.
- [Creating a Load Balancer](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/load-balancers/getting-started/creating-a-load-balancer/): Step-by-step guide to create and configure a Hetzner Load Balancer: location, type, network, targets, services, algorithm, labels, name.

### Certificates

- [Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/certificates/overview/): Overview of TLS/SSL certificates, upload existing or use Hetzner-managed Let's Encrypt with automatic renewal (Hetzner DNS required).
- [FAQ](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/certificates/faq/): Guide to managing HTTPS certificates in the Hetzner Console: create, upload, rename, delete.
- [Adding own certificates](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/certificates/getting-started/adding-certificates/): Step-by-step guide to upload and save a TLS/SSL certificate and private key in Hetzner Console.

### DNS

- [Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/overview/): Overview of Hetzner DNS: convert domains to IPs, manage zones and records, free of charge.
- [Features and Integrations](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/migration-to-hetzner-console/features-and-differences/): Explore new Hetzner DNS features: console and API integration, expanded record types, zone protection, comments, labels, and TSIG support.
- [General](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/faq/general/): Explains cross-project DNS zone sharing and how enabling 'Share zone with other projects' allows certificates/Load Balancers across projects.
- [Zones](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/faq/zones/): Subdomains are not supported; therefore, the domain <sub.domain.tld> cannot be created.
- [Records](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/faq/records/): Common DNS records to add after creating a zone, including A and MX examples for website and email setup.
- [Name servers](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/faq/nameservers/): Options to use your own or Hetzner Console DNS; avoid uppercase nameservers and reserved rDNS hostnames.
- [Creating a zone](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/getting-started/creating-a-zone/): Step-by-step guide to create, import, or configure primary/secondary DNS zones in Hetzner Console, including sharing and TSIG.
- [Updating name servers of external domains](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/getting-started/delegate-to-hetzner/): Instructions to delegate domains or add secondary Hetzner name servers and update external provider NS records; propagation may take 48 hours.
- [Adding records](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/getting-started/adding-records/): Step-by-step guide to add a DNS record in Hetzner Console: select zone, choose record type, fill fields, and click Add.
- [Managing name servers](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/getting-started/managing-name-servers/): How to edit external NS records in Hetzner Console; Hetzner NS entries are non-deletable and non-editable.
- [Editing the zone file](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/getting-started/editing-zone-files/): Step-by-step guide to edit and save a BIND-compatible DNS zone file in the Hetzner Console.
- [Configuring secondary zones for DNS software](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/howto-secondary-zones/dns-software/): Instructions for configuring self-managed primary name servers and Hetzner secondary name servers: Enable NOTIFY packets and AXFR/IXFR requests.
- [Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/overview/): Explains A, AAAA, HTTPS/SVCB and other DNS record types, their purposes and HTTPS record behavior.
- [A record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/a-record/): Explains A records mapping domains/subdomains to IPv4 addresses with example entries for root and subdomain.
- [AAAA record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/aaaa-record/): Defines AAAA DNS records that map (sub)domains to IPv6 addresses with examples.
- [CAA record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/caa-record/): Defines CAA DNS records and example entries specifying authorized CAs, reporting, and contact tags.
- [CNAME record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/cname-record/): Explains using CNAME records to point subdomains to other domains with an example (www → example.com).
- [DS record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/ds-record/): Explains Hetzner support for DS records only, with DS record fields and an example table and diagram.
- [HTTPS record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/https-record/): Explains HTTPS DNS records pointing domains to other domains and including connection parameters like ipv4 hints and ALPN.
- [MX record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/mx-record/): Explains MX records routing emails to mail server hostnames with A record example and setup links.
- [NS record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/ns-record/): Explains NS records pointing domains/subdomains to name server hostnames with delegation example.
- [PTR record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/ptr-record/): Explains PTR records for service discovery and reverse DNS with a DNS-SD example mapping services to instances.
- [SRV record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/srv-record/): Explains SRV records with example (Minecraft), showing fields: priority, weight, port, target, and A record mapping.
- [SVCB record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/svcb-record/): Explains SVCB DNS record usage with examples showing priority, targets, and parameters like alpn and IP hints.
- [TLSA record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/tlsa-record/): Explains TLSA usage: DNS records mapping services to certificate/public-key details with mail and web examples.
- [TXT record](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/record-types/txt-record/): Explains TXT record usage with examples for DMARC, SPF, ACME, and Google verification.
- [Architecture](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/technical-concepts/architecture/): Explains iterative vs recursive DNS queries and differences in resolver behavior.
- [Terminology](https://docs.hetzner.com/networking/dns/technical-concepts/terminology/): Human-readable internet names (domains), TLD types, registration and DNS zone management.

## Storage

### General

- [Which storage is right for me?](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/general/which-storage-is-right-for-me/): Comparison matrix of storage use cases across Object Storage, Storage Box, Storage Share, and Volumes.

### Object Storage

- [Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/overview/): S3-compatible object storage (immutable WORM) with buckets, pricing, endpoints, quotas, limits, and S3 API access.
- [List of supported actions](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/supported-actions/): Overview of Object Storage API S3-compatible features and notable unsupported bucket/object actions and limitations.
- [General](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/faq/general/): Overview of Hetzner S3-compatible Object Storage: buckets, object model, differences vs block storage, locations, redundancy, security.
- [S3 credentials](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/faq/s3-credentials/): Explains why both access and secret keys are required and their distinct purposes for requests.
- [Buckets & objects](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/faq/buckets-objects/): Access Buckets via Hetzner Console or S3-compatible tools using access and secret keys.
- [Generating S3 keys](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/generating-s3-keys/): Step-by-step guide to generate and securely save S3 access and secret keys in Hetzner Console.
- [Using S3 compatible CLI tools](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/using-s3-api-tools/): Guide to configure S3-compatible clients (mc, s3cmd, s5cmd, rclone, aws) with Hetzner Object Storage credentials and endpoints.
- [Using curl](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/using-curl/): Step-by-step curl S3 guide: create credentials, set env vars, manage buckets and objects with AWS SigV4.
- [Creating a Bucket](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/creating-a-bucket/): Step-by-step guide to create a unique Hetzner Object Storage bucket: location, name rules, and visibility options.
- [Creating a Bucket via MinIO Terraform Provider](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/creating-a-bucket-minio-terraform/): Guide to create an S3 bucket with aminueza/minio Terraform provider, using random UUID and private ACL.
- [Using libraries](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/using-libraries/): Python Boto3 example: create S3 client, random bucket name, create bucket and upload object.
- [Migrate a bucket from another provider to Hetzner Object Storage](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/getting-started/migrate-providers/): Step-by-step guide to migrate S3-compatible bucket data to Hetzner Object Storage using mc, rclone, s3cmd, or AWS CLI.
- [Custom domain with CNAME](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-configurations/domain-cname/): Guide to CNAME setup and host/SNI header overrides for using a custom domain with an object storage Bucket.
- [Custom domain with NGINX reverse proxy](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-configurations/domain-nginx/): Guide to configure NGINX reverse proxy on Debian to forward a custom domain to an object storage Bucket.
- [Custom domain with S3 Proxy](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-configurations/domain-s3-proxy/): Guide to forward a custom domain to an S3 Bucket using oxynozeta/s3-proxy with optional basic auth and Docker setup.
- [Cyberduck](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-local-storage-manager/cyberduck/): Guide to configuring Cyberduck for connecting to Hetzner S3 buckets and managing files via GUI.
- [WinSCP](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-local-storage-manager/winscp/): Guide to connect WinSCP to Amazon S3-compatible object storage (fsn1) for uploading and managing Buckets via GUI.
- [Versioning](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/protect-versioning/): Guide to enabling, checking, listing, retrieving, deleting, and suspending S3-compatible bucket versioning with MinIO and AWS CLI.
- [Object Lock: Legal Hold](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/protect-object-lock-legal-hold/): Guide to enable S3 Object Lock legal hold with MinIO AIStor Client and AWS CLI: create bucket, set/check/clear legal holds.
- [Object Lock: Retention](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/protect-object-lock-retention/): Guide to enable and manage S3 Object Lock retention using MinIO AIStor Client and AWS CLI with example commands.
- [Applying CORS policies](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/cors/): Guide to configure S3 CORS for Bucket access, with AWS CLI/S3cmd examples, presigned URLs, and verification steps.
- [Applying lifecycle policies](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/manage-lifecycle/): Guide to creating, applying, viewing, and removing S3/MinIO lifecycle policies to auto-delete objects (JSON/AWS CLI/MinIO commands).
- [Adding lifecycle policies via built-in MinIO commands](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/manage-lifecycle-built-in/): Guide to creating, applying, viewing, and removing S3/MinIO lifecycle policies to auto-delete objects (CLI/MinIO commands).
- [Encrypting data with SSE-C](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-protect-objects/encrypt-with-sse-c/): Guide to using SSE-C with MinIO/AWS CLI: generate/store keys, set env var, upload/download encrypted S3 objects.
- [Setting up Restic](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-backups/restic/): Guide to setting up Restic backups to object storage buckets with init, env vars, automation (resticprofile or cron).
- [Setting up Veeam](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-backups/veeam/): Guide: Configure Veeam Backup & Replication to use S3-compatible buckets with Hetzner, setup credentials, repository, registry keys.
- [Setting up Kopia CLI](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-backups/kopia-cli/): Guide to configure Kopia backups with S3-compatible Buckets: create credentials, repository, snapshots, restores, and cron automation.
- [Setting up Kopia GUI](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-backups/kopia-gui/): Guide to set up KopiaUI with Hetzner object storage buckets, create encrypted repositories, schedule and restore backups.
- [Setting up Duplicati](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-backups/duplicati/): Guide to set up Duplicati backups to S3-compatible Buckets (Hetzner): create credentials, install, configure, backup, and restore.
- [Setting up Bareos](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/howto-backups/bareos/): Guide to configure Bareos with Hetzner Object Storage, including credentials, PostgreSQL, S3 tools, and device/storage setup.
- [Bandwidth or latency issues](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/troubleshooting/bandwidth-latency-issues/): Troubleshoot Object Storage bandwidth/latency: run mtr to trace routes and curl/wget speed tests, include outputs for support.
- [HTTP 400](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/object-storage/troubleshooting/http-400/): Troubleshoot HTTP 400 errors: check upload inactivity timeouts and ensure Host header matches the Bucket domain.

### Storage Box

- [Storage Box Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/general/): Managed redundant Storage Box with RAID, multiple access protocols, SSH keys, snapshots, sub-accounts, pricing and usage limits.
- [Storage Box Snapshots](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/snapshots/): Explanation of Storage Box snapshots: types, behavior on restore, storage usage, visibility, limits and pricing.
- [Determine available Storage Box disk space](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/available-disk-space/): Methods to check available Storage Box disk space via Hetzner Console, SFTP, SSH, lftp, or Hetzner API.
- [Storage Box FAQ](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/faq/faq/): Check that the required protocol is enabled for your Storage Box in Hetzner Console settings.
- [Storage Box vs Storage Share](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/faq/storage-box-vs-storage-share/): Comparison table summarizing Storage Box vs Storage Share features, protocols, and capabilities.
- [Creating Storage Box snapshots](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/getting-started/creating-snapshots/): How to create manual or enable automatic snapshots for a Storage Box via the Hetzner Console.
- [Creating a Storage Box](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/getting-started/creating-a-storage-box/): Step-by-step guide to create and configure a Hetzner Storage Box: location, type, access, protocols, labels, and name.
- [Storage Box Access Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/access/access-overview/): Storage Box connection details: hostnames, usernames, ports for FTP/FTPS, SFTP/SCP, rsync, SMB/CIFS, HTTPS/WebDAV.
- [Access with FTP/FTPS](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/access/access-ftp-ftps/): Guide to connecting an FTPS Storage Box in Windows Explorer, explaining FTP modes, security, and setup steps.
- [Access with SFTP/SCP](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/access/access-sftp-scp/): Guide to connecting to a Storage Box via encrypted SFTP/SCP, including software, hostnames, SSH keys, and fingerprint verification.
- [Access with SSH/rsync/BorgBackup](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/access/access-ssh-rsync-borg/): Enabling and connecting to the extended SSH service on port 23, SSH key authentication in OpenSSH format, and using relative paths on the Storage Box.
- [Access with SMB/CIFS](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/access/access-smb-cifs/): Guide to mount Hetzner Storage Box via SMB/CIFS on Linux, FreeBSD, or Windows with setup and fstab instructions.
- [Access with WebDAV](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/access/access-webdav/): Guide to enable and mount Hetzner Storage Box via WebDAV on Linux and Windows, including setup and known issues.
- [Add SSH Keys](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/ssh-keys/add-ssh-keys/): Step-by-step guide to generate, convert (RFC4716), upload and test SSH public keys for Hetzner Storage Box access.

### Storage Share

- [General](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/general/): Overview and features of Hetzner Storage Share (Nextcloud): access, apps, file browser, navigation, upload and sharing basics.
- [Desktop / Mobile Client](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/configuration/desktop-mobile-client/): Lists desktop and mobile Nextcloud clients with download links and login instructions for Hetzner Storage Share.
- [Mount external storage](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/configuration/external-storage/): Guide to configuring Hetzner Storage Box as external storage (SMB, SFTP, FTP/S, WebDAV) in Storage Share v24.0.3.
- [OCC Commands](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/configuration/occ-commands/): Guide to using Nextcloud’s OCC CLI in konsoleH: locating, executing commands, warnings, troubleshooting inaccessible instances, and requesting unsupported commands.
- [Subdomains](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/configuration/subdomain/): Guide to assign a custom CNAME subdomain in konsoleH and speed up SSL setup with Let's Encrypt.
- [Additional apps](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/additional-apps/): Instructions for activating apps and using OnlyOffice or Collabora via self-hosted servers; no provider support.
- [Backups / Snapshots](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/backup-snapshot/): Backups occur automatically multiple times daily; manual backups unavailable.
- [Other Questions](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/other/): Link to detailed comparison between Storage Box and Storage Share.
- [Security](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/security/): Explains redundancy, integrity checks, drive replacement, and high-availability clustering for Storage Share data security.
- [Subdomain](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/subdomain/): Allows using custom subdomains with NX11+ by adding CNAMEs; main domains limited and Let's Encrypt SSL handled automatically.
- [Update / Upgrade](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/upgrade/): Hetzner automatically applies tested Nextcloud updates; customers see but cannot install notices.
- [Upload, edit and share files](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/upload-edit-share-files/): Upload files using the + button or drag-and-drop if your browser supports it.
- [User accounts and groups](https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-share/faq/user-accounts-groups/): Yes — an administration account is provided and allows customization and activation of additional apps.

## General

### Billing and Account Management

- [Hetzner Account Getting Started](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/account-getting-started/): Step-by-step account registration guide covering requirements, email verification, and dashboard navigation.
- [Product migration](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/product-migration/): Robot transfers: dedicated servers via docs link, domain token flow (7-day validity), rackspot form/ticket options, vSwitches non-transferable.
- [Payment Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/billing-at-hetzner/payment-overview/): Accepted methods: VISA/Mastercard/AMEX/UnionPay credit cards, SEPA for EUR accounts, bank transfer, PayPal; no Apple Pay, no partial plans.
- [Billing system at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/billing-at-hetzner/billing-system-hetzner/): Pro-rated billing charges after usage, switching from hourly to monthly rates, with invoices covering the previous month.
- [Promo codes on your Hetzner account](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/billing-at-hetzner/promo-code/): Definition of promo codes as credit or discount codes, plus move from Hetzner Console Usage view to central User account management.
- [Value added tax](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/billing-at-hetzner/value-added-tax/): VAT rules by residence: 19% for Germany, EU reverse-charge with valid VAT ID, country-specific EU/non-EU rate tables and US exemption certificates.
- [Overview – Canceling products and contracts with Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/cancellation/cancellations-overview/): Four core rules: users must actively cancel, billing stays pro-rated with monthly cap, notice periods vary, and data is deleted after cancellation.
- [Cancellations of managed products via konsoleH](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/cancellation/cancellations-managed-products/): Log in to konsoleH.hetzner.com with customer number and password to see all products grouped by category.
- [Cancellations on Hetzner Console](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/cancellation/cancellations-hetzner-console/): Log in at console.hetzner.com/projects and open the project containing the resource you want to cancel.
- [Cancellations on Robot](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/cancellation/cancellations-robot/): Robot login at robot.hetzner.com and selection of the correct product category from the left menu.
- [30 days to the end of the month policy](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/billing-and-account-management/cancellation/30-days-to-the-end-of-the-month/): Explains the 30-day-to-end-of-month cancellation policy, billing rules, and account termination examples.

### Company and Policy

- [Data Protection at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/data-protection-at-hetzner/): Reasons for account deactivation (inactivity, unpaid invoices) and step-by-step process to delete an account after cancellation.
- [Hetzner customer newsletter](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/customer-newsletter/): Roughly monthly Hetzner customer newsletter covering sales, product launches, network updates, OS/software notices, beta invitations and security warnings, with signup and unsubscribe links.
- [Hetzner Forum](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/hetzner-forum/): Customer-only Hetzner Forum for beta announcements, peer troubleshooting, Marktplatz dedicated-server transfers, and IT discussions in English or German.
- [Information security at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/information-security-at-hetzner/): Link to ISO/IEC 27001:2022 certificate PDF and note that internal SoA has no Annex A exclusions.
- [Legal requirements for websites – basics of the legal notice](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/basics-of-the-legal-notice/): Purpose of a legal notice: naming the responsible provider and enabling contact for copyright, spam or complaint matters.
- [Service Level Agreement (SLA) for Cloud servers](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/slas-cloud/): Cloud Server SLA guaranteeing 99.9% monthly availability with a worked example of Cloud Credit compensation for downtime beyond the threshold.
- [Sustainability at Hetzner](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/sustainability-at-hetzner/): Hetzner holds EMAS and ISO 14001 certifications for transparent environmental management and continuous sustainability improvement.
- [Experiments platform - Overview](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/experiments/experiments-platform/): Experiments platform hosting a free Inference API with an Open-Weight LLM and a fully hosted OpenClaw assistant, without guarantees or backups.
- [Inference API](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/company-and-policy/experiments/inference/): OpenAI-compatible Inference API at inference.hetzner.com with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8 model, Python/curl chat and vision examples, per-key rate limits and API-token FAQ.

### Security and Identification

- [Abuse form](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/abuse-form/): Link to Hetzner's Abuse Team report form with instructions to file one submission per individual case.
- [Fraud prevention FAQ](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/fraud-prevention-faq/): Purpose of Hetzner's fraud prevention: protect systems and customers by verifying that account and order data is authentic.
- [Login-OTP](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/login-otp/): Five-step flow from login attempt through device/location check, 6-digit email code delivery, entry, and access; 2FA supersedes it.
- [Phishing email collection](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/phishing-email-collection/): Phishing messages mimic trusted senders and pressure recipients into revealing data or opening links and attachments.
- [Support OTP](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/support-otp/): Benefits: real-time phone contact with support, no Robot login needed, and no pre-set telephone password required.
- [Technical and Organizational Measures](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/technical-and-organizational-measures/): Site entry controls: logged badge access, video surveillance, visitor policy, perimeter fencing, and lockable colocation racks.
- [Two-factor authentication](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/security-and-identify/two-factor-authentication/): Six-step walkthrough to enable 2FA in Hetzner Accounts, note the recovery key, and add an authentication method.

### Infrastructure and availability

- [Data centers and connection](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/data-centers-and-connection/): Definition of the term data center (DC) covering the building, hosted servers, and operating organization.
- [Hetzner Price Adjustment 15 June 2026](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/price-adjustment/): New monthly and setup prices for AX, EX, SX, GEX, DX dedicated servers in Falkenstein, Nuremberg and Helsinki plus limited-tier offerings.
- [Hetzner pricing structure explained](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/hetzner-pricing-structure-explained/): How owning land and data centers, building servers in-house with carefully chosen components, and cost-aligned setup fees drive Hetzner's price/performance ratio.
- [IP pricing](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/ipv4-pricing/): Monthly and setup fees in EUR/USD for primary IPv4, additional IPs, /29–/24 subnets, failover IPs and /64 IPv6 failover on dedicated servers.
- [Order processing](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/order-processing/): Weekly-updated provisioning time estimates for AX, EX, SX, GEX, DX and managed products in German and Finnish locations, with notes on limited and 10 Gbit uplink orders.
- [Peering Policy](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/peering-policy/): Open peering policy with private peerings in 10 cities (100/400 Gbit/s), public peerings via AS24940, and Tier 1/2 IP transit partners.
- [Standardization and price adjustment FAQ](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/faq-standardization-and-price-adjustment/): Move to up to three fixed RAM/storage configurations based on top ~90% of orders, with Custom Solutions still available and Dell servers retained.
- [Support Team opening hours](https://docs.hetzner.com/general/infrastructure-and-availability/support-team-opening-hours/): General enquiries Mon–Fri 8 a.m.–6 p.m. CET, 24/7 ticket support for cloud and data center technician tasks, submitted via Robot, Console or konsoleH.

## Optional

- [Hetzner API overview](https://docs.hetzner.cloud/): Cloud API, Storage Box API and the `hcloud` CLI.
- [Robot Web Service](https://robot.hetzner.com/doc/webservice/en.html#preface): REST API for dedicated servers. Separate from the Cloud API, with separate credentials.
- [Hetzner Community tutorials](https://community.hetzner.com/tutorials/): Community-contributed, editorially reviewed guides. Useful for end-to-end setups, not normative for product behaviour.
- [Hetzner Support Center](https://www.hetzner.com/support/): Support channels, business hours, forum and status page.
- [Hetzner website](https://www.hetzner.com/): Current products, prices and specifications.
